From a62f64c551ba97fa539094356a12f3a93724f5bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: build <build@localhost>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 01:03:51 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Decode into the dma-bufs a client exported before the first
 decode

GStreamer's va dma-buf allocator creates each surface and exports it in
one step, then keeps those fds (and the plane layout from the
descriptor) for the life of the buffer. This driver treated any export
before a surface's first decode as probing: it backed the surface with
a throwaway buffer and freed it once the decode bound the surface to its
own MMAP CAPTURE buffer. Every frame went to memory the client never
saw. Through kmssink and glimagesink the picture was solid green (a
zeroed NV12 buffer) at a steady 30 fps; only readback (vaGetImage) was
right, which is all the regression checks looked at.

The CAPTURE queue's memory type is now chosen by its first buffer. When
the first surface bound to a context was already exported, and that
export fits the negotiated CAPTURE format, the queue imports dma-bufs:
each surface's backing becomes the memory of its CAPTURE buffer (the
inverse of the adopt path that keeps frames alive past their context).
A surface with no backing, or with backing that does not fit, gets new
backing from a throwaway open of the same decoder in the context's own
formats, with a message when a client is left holding a stale export.

The fit test matters: FFmpeg probes one surface by exporting it before
any decode, at the surface size, and on the AV1 core (which pads the
height and appends its own data to each buffer) that probe never fits.
FFmpeg therefore keeps the decoder's MMAP buffers, as before.

So the layout exported up front matches what the decoder writes:
standalone backing asks for the same 64-byte NV12 pitch as the decode
format, and honours V4L2_REQUEST_SCALE, the H713 decode-time scaler.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Origin: https://github.com/cstenger/allwinner-h713-mainline/blob/43b2cdd4aa1b161a281db8b10f02ce70085e2d42/patches/libva-v4l2_request/0007-Decode-into-the-dma-bufs-a-client-exported-before-th.patch (0007-Decode-into-the-dma-bufs-a-client-exported-before-th.patch, commit 7552704)
